# Lentil & Sweet Potato Chile

Adapted from lentils.md research document

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] Optional: 1 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } for sauteing
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 1 [bell pepper]{ ing="bell-pepper" }, diced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }
- [ ] 1 cup [green or brown lentils]{ ing="green-or-brown-lentils" }, rinsed
- [ ] 2 medium [sweet potatoes]{ ing="sweet-potatoes" }, peeled and cubed (about 3 cups)
- [ ] 1 (14 oz) can [crushed tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 2 cups [vegetable broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } to taste

### For Serving

- [ ] [Greek yogurt]{ ing="greek-yogurt" } or sour cream
- [ ] [Avocado slices]{ ing="avocado-slices" }
- [ ] [Pepitas]{ ing="pepitas" } (pumpkin seeds)
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

## Recipe

1. (Optional) Saute [onion]{ ing="onion" } and [bell pepper]{ ing="bell-pepper" } in [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in Instant Pot on saute mode for 3-4 minutes
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }, cook for 1 minute
1. Add [lentils]{ ing="green-or-brown-lentils" }, sweet potato cubes, [crushed tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }, [broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }, and all spices
1. Cook on high pressure for 10 minutes
1. Quick release pressure
1. Season with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } to taste
1. Serve with desired toppings

## Notes

- Lentils mimic ground meat texture while sweet potato adds natural sweetness and creaminess
- Green or brown lentils maintain firm texture and add peppery flavor that balances the sweet potato; red lentils would break down too much for this dish
- Can add cooked ground turkey for extra protein if desired
- Adjust spice levels to taste; this version is mild
- For creamier texture, mash some of the sweet potato after cooking
- Freezes well for meal prep
